# Each canary makes up its own addresses, under a folder named for its check.
# Those addresses are never in the model, so nothing defines them there. The
# canary is what describes them, so the site sends the whole folder to the
# published canary with a 303. A made-up file name outside a canary's folder
# stays a 404: the file does not exist, and saying so is the canary's point.
<https://drift-king.org/the-linter/canaries/approvals-are-documents.ttl> a prov:Entity ;
