# The Cloudflare account, named by the setting it is read from and never by
# its value: the value lives only in the environment of whoever ships, so no
# file of ours, and nothing drift-king.org publishes, holds it. A step that
# needs it fails before it runs when the setting is empty.
<https://drift-king.org/not-ah/setting/user-profile>
    rdfs:label "USERPROFILE" ;
    rdfs:comment "The folder of the user who builds, read from the environment by name. It goes into the cargo config the build writes, and into nothing that is committed or published." .
<https://drift-king.org/not-ah/setting/cloudflare-account-id>
    rdfs:label "CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID" ;
    rdfs:comment "The Cloudflare account the registry and the Worker belong to. Read from the environment by name; wrangler reads the same variable itself." .

